			"date": "2023-06-09T23:37:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://masto.ai/@litherum\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>litherum</span></a></span> \"We’ll continue to be profit-driven until profits arrive,\" sounds a whole lot like \"The beatings will continue until morale improves.\"</p><p>At this point I'm probably going to be down to just Discord and the Fediverse when Reddit's API pricing goes into effect. Hopefully Discord makes enough from Nitro so they won't get greedy about their API like Reddit and Twitter. If they start charging bot devs, I'm gone. I make exactly zero dollars from my Discord bot but if I have to pay to keep it running I'm taking it down.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
